<!doctype html><html><head><title>Zero Web diagnostic page</title><style>body { background-color: #edf2f7; padding: 12px; } h1 { color: #243047; font-size: 24px; margin: 8px; } p { color: #bb0000; font-size: 16px; margin: 4px; } .sample { color: #00aa00; } #identity { color: #0000bb; } #inline { color: #0000bb; } .sample { color: #008800; } .hidden { display: none; } .note { color: #243047; } .card { background-color: #ffffff; padding: 8px; margin: 8px; } #script { color: #0f766e; }</style></head><body><h1>Zero Web diagnostic page</h1><div class=card><p class=note>CSS priority: compare these labels with their colors.</p><p>TAG: red bb0000.</p><p class=sample>CLASS: green 008800; later equal-specificity rule wins.</p><p id=identity class=sample>ID: blue 0000bb; id beats a later class rule.</p><p id=inline class=sample style='color: #aa00aa;'>INLINE: purple aa00aa; inline beats id and class rules.</p></div><div class=card><p class=note>Display test: only the VISIBLE marker must appear below.</p><p class=hidden>HIDDEN_SENTINEL</p><p class=note>VISIBLE</p><p class=note>BR first line.<br>BR second line.</p><p class=note>Those BR labels must appear on separate lines.</p></div><div class=card><p class=note>Script test: the following line must start with PASS.</p><p id=script>Pending script replacement.</p><p class=note>This is an original bounded-profile fixture, not a full browser conformance test.</p></div><script>const count = 1 + 2; let message = 'PASS: textContent replaced this line; 1 + 2 = '; document.getElementById('script').textContent = message + count;</script></body></html>